{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And HaShem saw that Leah was hated.</b> It intends to say that HaShem alone is the One who knew and recognized that she was hated — not so she herself, for she did not feel her being hated, but rather thought only that she was not loved, as I will explain from her words nearby. And our Sages of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 71:2) said: <b>hated</b> — that people would say, 'This is the wife of the hated one,' that is, Esau, for it is written (Malachi 1:3) ״וְאֶת עֵשָׂו שָׂנֵאתִי״, and she was called by his name. And accordingly, if she had no children, they would have confirmed the matter — that she is not Jacob's proper mate; therefore <b>and He opened her womb.</b> And the verse saying <b>but Rachel was barren</b> means: all the more so, and perhaps it would remove her being hated — that this one does not give birth and that one does give birth."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:56.457740294Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}